    schema:about "Xenopus laevis & Gallus gallus vertebrate paraxial mesoderm somites" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: The published 3-4 variable Goldbeter (2007) kinetics with explicit Cyp26 / Raldh2, quantitative reproduction of its hysteresis figures or of Dubrulle (2001) somite sizes, T1 transitions / epithelial rosette formation / apical constriction, the 90-degree Xenopus somite cell-block rotation, 3D epithelialisation mechanics, or explicit Delta-Notch intercellular delay coupling (Slots 022-023)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 1D anteroposterior Thom-Zeeman cusp catastrophe ODE tau_chi*dchi/dt = -(chi^3 - a(x,t)*chi - b_osc(x,t)) with either the prescribed kinematic front a = tanh((v t - x)/sigma_w) or the Goldbeter FGF/RA toggle front a = tanh((R - F)/kappa_a), m = F^4/(F^4 + K_mob^4), driven by tailbud elongation through M_F = exp(-(x_tb - x)/lambda_F), lambda_F = v_tb/k_dM (reduced two-variable toggle; Cyp26/Raldh2 lumped)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak and inter-somitic cleft segmentation on somite_embryo_specimen.jpg (48.47 px mean spacing, symmetry ratio 0.9605) plus a per-cleft luminance-minimum line fit giving an empirical cleft angle of 7.9 deg",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Endogenous front velocity fit (v_front = 2.22222 um/min vs v_tb = 2.2222, R^2 = 1.000), 4-point v_tb sweep (S RMSE 0.09 um), decaying-Gaussian FGF8 bead perturbation (min adjacent somite ratio 0.70, max 1.55)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Farhadifar vertex model of a 60 x 6 hexagonal PSM sheet (20 um pitch, Lambda_0 = 0.12, Gamma = 0.04, dLambda_cleft = 0.9, outer boundary pinned, gradient descent, no T1) in which only posterior(-1)->anterior(+1) half-somite interfaces are loaded: 12 clefts at 100.0 um pitch, cleft angle 28.2 -> 10.3 deg (control 27.3), tortuosity 1.30 -> 1.03, shape index 3.76",
        "reported_in_source: Cooke & Zeeman (1976) J. Theor. Biol. 58:455-476 kinematic somite wavelength law S = v * T_c and Thom-Zeeman cusp catastrophe wavefront manifold",
        "reported_in_source: Cooke (1975) Nature 254:196-199 Xenopus laevis blastula size-reduction invariance (N ~ 40 somites across normal and miniature embryos)",
        "reported_in_source: Dubrulle, McGrew & Pourquie (2001) Cell 106:219-232: an ectopic FGF8 bead produces smaller somites at its level (no numerical ratio reported)",
        "reported_in_source: Farhadifar et al. (2007) Curr. Biol. 17:2095-2104 vertex-model energy and case-I parameters; Bi et al. (2015) Nat. Phys. 11:1074-1079 shape-index rigidity transition p0* = 3.81",
        "reported_in_source: Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquie (2007) Dev. Dyn. 236:1495-1508: mutual FGF/RA inhibition is bistable and its switching threshold defines a sharp determination front that moves with axis elongation; Dubrulle & Pourquie (2004) Nature 427:419-422: the fgf8 gradient is set by mRNA decay in cells leaving the tailbud",
        "transfer_boundary: 1D anteroposterior paraxial mesoderm axis mapped to dorsal vertebrate SEM somite rows; the specimen is a chick SEM in pixels with no scale bar, so S_obs (px) is compared to the Cooke-Zeeman waveform shape and cleft orientation only, not to S_sim in um",
        "transfer_boundary: The FGF/RA toggle parameters (alpha = 3, K = 1, n = 4, tau_FR = 12 min, k_dM = 0.0074/min) are tuned to place the front offset ~0.19 mm behind the tailbud; they are not Goldbeter et al.'s published kinetic constants, so only the qualitative predictions (bistability, v_front = v_tb, bead effect) are tested",
        "transfer_boundary: The chi = +1 / -1 compartments of the cusp are read as anterior / posterior half-somites (Saga & Takeda 2001) to decide which interfaces are clefts; Cooke & Zeeman themselves did not make this identification" ;
